From: TekRantGaming <craigferels896@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 17:50:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] D3D12: AO prototype at half resolution, GPU timing, fixes

Works the AO out once a frame at half resolution (depth, AO, separable blur, edge-aware upsample) and only multiplies it in at each scene copy. Compact formats where UAV typed loads allow. Adds a UAV barrier before reading the dumped depth (uncapped frame rates read it too early), applies only to copies to the frame's first scene destination (not the final image), and dumps the depth once a frame. REX_DEV_AO_STATS logs per-pass GPU time; REX_DEV_AO_TOGGLE and REX_DEV_AO_TRACE for testing.

